From: TB522FU Debian port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: keep TB522FU firmware display power

The borrowed framebuffer had no power-domain consumer. RAM controls kept
GNOME visible while multimedia clock providers remained unbound. Binding
the last provider completed RPMh sync_state and the physical panel went
black while the compositor continued rendering.

Declare MMCX at NOM_L1. The stock display driver maps its maximum 575 MHz
MDP clock to level 320, matching the upstream SoC OPP. Native display/GPU
remain disabled; no clock rate or panel command changes. Allow the generic
required-opps property in the simple-framebuffer binding.

Hardware verification of this correction is pending.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
@@ -494,3 +494,12 @@
 
 /* Stock GPI1 mask 0x1e, SE4, stream ID 0xb6; no other serial engines enabled. */
 &gpi_dma1 { status = "okay"; };
+
+/* Borrowed scanout must own MMCX before provider sync drops boot votes.
+ * Stock maximum MDP rate 575 MHz requires RPMh level 320 (NOM_L1).
+ * This keeps power only; it does not program display clocks or the panel.
+ */
+&{/framebuffer@fc800000} {
+	power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_MMCX>;
+	required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_nom_l1>;
+};
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/simple-framebuffer.yaml
@@ -78,6 +78,9 @@
 
   power-domains:
     description: List of power domains used by the framebuffer.
+
+  required-opps:
+    description: Performance states needed by the framebuffer power domains.
 
   width:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
